\n- adapter.py (14): D:module@1-37, D:_message_tag@92-95, D:_coverage_gap_reason@103-106, D:_translate_findings@122-134, D:ReviewedTreeMismatch@221-224, D:_resolve_reviewed_head@237-244, D:_assert_reviewed_tree@260-273, D:code_review_decision@311-324, D:append_retries_exhausted_note@412-415, C:module@76-83, C:_translate_findings@148-151, C:module@230-232, C:code_review_decision@338-340, C:code_review_decision@404-407.\n- app.py (25): D:module@1-31, D:_install_offload_executor@117-121, D:_running_offload_threads@128-132, D:_force_process_exit@141-145, D:_arm_hard_shutdown@158-164, D:_request_token@199-205, D:_current_revision@413-424, D:_superseded_by@442-446, D:_worker@457-464, D:_discard_superseded@538-542, C:module@70-77, C:module@91-112, C:module@171-180, C:lifespan@300-304, C:lifespan@317-328, C:lifespan@341-360, C:lifespan@365-373, C:lifespan@380-387, C:lifespan@389-400, C:_worker@469-472, C:_worker@485-496, C:_worker@512-515, C:module@564-567, C:module@570-574, C:rerun@721-723.\n- config.py (13): D:module@1-20, D:review_timeout_seconds@86-91, D:shutdown_force_exit_grace_seconds@132-153, D:configure_logging@161-186, D:TokenRedactingFilter@222-230, D:install_access_log_redaction@244-249, C:module@35-51, C:module@54-64, C:module@67-71, C:module@74-77, C:module@204-210, C:ReceiverConfig@295-304, C:ReceiverConfig@308-312.\n- finding_publish.py (9): D:module@1-29, D:parse_anchor@64-74, D:partition_findings@91-97, D:_standing_suffix@120-123, D:render_findings_block@141-147, D:build_inline_comments@162-167, D:post_review@205-213, C:module@50-52, C:module@109-112.\n- gerrit_client.py (19): D:module@1-22, D:_git_op@71-75, D:GerritClient.get_patch@145-151, D:GerritClient.get_merge_files@193-197, D:GerritClient.get_revision_files@201-207, D:GerritClient.has_llm_review_vote@226-231, D:GerritClient.reset_llm_review_vote@244-250, D:GerritClient.get_change_event@267-273, D:GerritClient.post_vote@304-317, D:GerritClient.get_change_messages@349-354, D:GerritClient.post_comment@359-365, D:GerritClient.list_events@411-421, D:GerritClient.clone_change_ref@439-444, D:GerritClient._redact@544-546, C:module@44-58, C:GerritClient@175-183, C:GerritClient.clone_change_ref@489-496, C:GerritClient.clone_change_ref@523-525, C:GerritClient.clone_change_ref@533-535.\n- low_disk.py (5): D:module@1-27, D:scratch_unavailable_detail@76-84, D:scratch_coverage@91-96, D:pre_clone_refusal@120-126, D:review_clone_has_room@140-145.\n- reconcile.py (13): D:module@1-51, D:_degraded@148-153, D:_write_cursor@172-179, D:_candidate_events@211-219, D:reconcile_once@268-278, D:_persist_cursor@397-407, D:reconcile_loop@443-452, C:module@75-88, C:module@91-105, C:_candidate_events@228-232, C:reconcile_once@307-309, C:reconcile_once@313-323, C:reconcile_once@358-363.\n- retrigger.py (18): D:module@1-35, D:classify_tag@91-98, D:latest_bot_message@134-138, D:sole_blocking_criterion@153-157, D:attestation_now_acceptable@185-197, D:latest_bot_tag_state@226-233, D:_actionable_change_key@283-286, D:_refuse_retired_word@308-313, D:handle_comment_added@353-361, C:module@51-55, C:module@62-64, C:module@67-69, C:module@76-79, C:module@115-118, C:module@121-124, C:_refusal_message@256-258, C:module@271-273, C:handle_comment_added@426-430.\n- voter.py (25): D:module@1-22, D:in_flight_reviews@97-104, D:_voter_error@136-139, D:_publish_voter_error_metric@159-163, D:_publish_token_usage_metrics@189-195, D:_emit_token_usage@215-220, D:_extract@238-242, D:review_and_vote@272-283, D:_decision_for_clone@300-308, D:_guard_decision_auth@400-403, D:_resolve_review_runtime@413-416, D:_handle_retryable_gap@429-433, D:_superseded_before_vote@511-518, C:module@64-71, C:module@75-92, C:module@175-178, C:_decision_for_clone@323-326, C:_review_and_vote@616-623, C:_review_and_vote@633-636, C:_review_and_vote@663-666, C:_review_and_vote@701-708, C:_review_and_vote@712-715, C:_review_and_vote@727-730, C:_review_and_vote@765-767, C:_review_and_vote@775-783.\n\n## Contracts, consumers, and exclusions\nPreserve optional-import boundaries; four-pass verdict/coverage mapping; reviewed-tree-to-vote binding; header-first authentication; fast ACK, bounded drain/cancel, and hard-exit sequencing; cursor low-water recovery; merge-delta REST behavior; token redaction; the shared low-disk no-vote route; privileged retrigger eligibility/reset; pre-vote staleness suppression; and post-vote artifact capture. Consumers include the FastAPI service, Gerrit REST, autodeploy/observability scripts, and review-bot tests. The health, webhook, and rerun route docstrings are excluded because FastAPI publishes them through OpenAPI.\n\nConcise/load-bearing prose outside the allowlist stays byte-identical. So do runtime strings, assertions, fixtures, decorators, subprocess arguments, config values, and all 25 directive/shebang physical lines. All files are Python.\n\n## Verification and independent review\nParse base and final Python with `type_comments=True`; replace only allowlisted leading owner docstrings, normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`, and require the remaining AST/runtime tree to match. A zero-context base-to-final hunk guard restricts every deletion/insertion to an exact allowlisted base span. Run all six structured DD commands, including exact grouped-commit paths and the generated environment-registry citation, focused consumers, scoped diff integrity, hygiene, and untimed worktree-venv `make verify`.\n\nA reviewer who did not author the patch records a leaf-linked TSV with exactly 142 PASS rows, one per stable ID: `stable_id,before_citation,final_citation,preserved_contract_or_consumer,directives_exact,before_words,final_words,reviewer_session,semantic_pass,bloat_pass`. Every `final_words` is smaller; missing, extra, duplicate, or FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly 142 allowlisted blocks have smaller final word counts.\n- [ ] Non-allowlisted prose and all 25 directive/shebang lines remain exact.\n- [ ] The immutable-base runtime/non-comment oracle passes for every owned file.\n- [ ] Every preserved contract or consumer has an independent TSV PASS citation.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the grouped 28 declared paths and focused, diff-integrity, and hygiene checks exit 0.\n- [ ] Untimed worktree-venv `make verify` exits 0.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/__init__.py","reason":"Condense 1 package-responsibility/import-boundary docstring; preserve optional-dependency behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py","reason":"Condense 14 verdict, coverage-gap, finding, and tree-binding blocks; preserve fail-closed label semantics."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","reason":"Condense 25 auth, shutdown, queue, and staleness blocks; protect OpenAPI route docstrings and directives."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/config.py","reason":"Condense 13 timeout, drain, logging, redaction, and cursor blocks; preserve budget relationships."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py","reason":"Condense 9 anchor, rendering, and publication blocks; preserve message/inline fallback visibility."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py","reason":"Condense 19 REST, merge-delta, fetch, and redaction blocks; preserve wire contracts and token safety."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py","reason":"Condense 5 disk-admission blocks; preserve the shared low-disk retry/no-vote routing contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py","reason":"Condense 13 cursor, retry, and cooperative-drain blocks; preserve low-water recovery."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py","reason":"Condense 18 trigger, tag, eligibility, and reset blocks; preserve privileged fail-closed decisions."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py","reason":"Condense 25 single-flight, merge, staleness, voting, and artifact blocks; preserve no-dishonest-vote behavior."},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Regenerate the one review_bot/config.py dynamic environment-read line citation after scoped prose shrinks."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6","parent_status_uuid":"3825287d-bcd6-4aba-b923-0bd733be54d0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"84f2-67b7-9d06-4a7e","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in src/rebar/review_bot","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c '\nimport ast, io, re, subprocess, tokenize\nfrom pathlib import Path\nB = \"cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a\"\nDOCS = {\"src/rebar/review_bot/__init__.py\":[\"module\"],\"src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py\":[\"module\",\"_message_tag\",\"_coverage_gap_reason\",\"_translate_findings\",\"ReviewedTreeMismatch\",\"_resolve_reviewed_head\",\"_assert_reviewed_tree\",\"code_review_decision\",\"append_retries_exhausted_note\"],\"src/rebar/review_bot/app.py\":[\"module\",\"_install_offload_executor\",\"_running_offload_threads\",\"_force_process_exit\",\"_arm_hard_shutdown\",\"_request_token\",\"_current_revision\",\"_superseded_by\",\"_worker\",\"_discard_superseded\"],\"src/rebar/review_bot/config.py\":[\"module\",\"review_timeout_seconds\",\"shutdown_force_exit_grace_seconds\",\"configure_logging\",\"TokenRedactingFilter\",\"install_access_log_redaction\"],\"src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py\":[\"module\",\"parse_anchor\",\"partition_findings\",\"_standing_suffix\",\"render_findings_block\",\"build_inline_comments\",\"post_review\"],\"src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py\":[\"module\",\"_git_op\",\"GerritClient.get_patch\",\"GerritClient.get_merge_files\",\"GerritClient.get_revision_files\",\"GerritClient.has_llm_review_vote\",\"GerritClient.reset_llm_review_vote\",\"GerritClient.get_change_event\",\"GerritClient.post_vote\",\"GerritClient.get_change_messages\",\"GerritClient.post_comment\",\"GerritClient.list_events\",\"GerritClient.clone_change_ref\",\"GerritClient._redact\"],\"src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py\":[\"module\",\"scratch_unavailable_detail\",\"scratch_coverage\",\"pre_clone_refusal\",\"review_clone_has_room\"],\"src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py\":[\"module\",\"_degraded\",\"_write_cursor\",\"_candidate_events\",\"reconcile_once\",\"_persist_cursor\",\"reconcile_loop\"],\"src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py\":[\"module\",\"classify_tag\",\"latest_bot_message\",\"sole_blocking_criterion\",\"attestation_now_acceptable\",\"latest_bot_tag_state\",\"_actionable_change_key\",\"_refuse_retired_word\",\"handle_comment_added\"],\"src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py\":[\"module\",\"in_flight_reviews\",\"_voter_error\",\"_publish_voter_error_metric\",\"_publish_token_usage_metrics\",\"_emit_token_usage\",\"_extract\",\"review_and_vote\",\"_decision_for_clone\",\"_guard_decision_auth\",\"_resolve_review_runtime\",\"_handle_retryable_gap\",\"_superseded_before_vote\"]}\nSPANS = {\"src/rebar/review_bot/__init__.py\":[[1,17]],\"src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py\":[[1,37],[92,95],[103,106],[122,134],[221,224],[237,244],[260,273],[311,324],[412,415],[76,83],[148,151],[230,232],[338,340],[404,407]],\"src/rebar/review_bot/app.py\":[[1,31],[117,121],[128,132],[141,145],[158,164],[199,205],[413,424],[442,446],[457,464],[538,542],[70,77],[91,112],[171,180],[300,304],[317,328],[341,360],[365,373],[380,387],[389,400],[469,472],[485,496],[512,515],[564,567],[570,574],[721,723]],\"src/rebar/review_bot/config.py\":[[1,20],[86,91],[132,153],[161,186],[222,230],[244,249],[35,51],[54,64],[67,71],[74,77],[204,210],[295,304],[308,312]],\"src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py\":[[1,29],[64,74],[91,97],[120,123],[141,147],[162,167],[205,213],[50,52],[109,112]],\"src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py\":[[1,22],[71,75],[145,151],[193,197],[201,207],[226,231],[244,250],[267,273],[304,317],[349,354],[359,365],[411,421],[439,444],[544,546],[44,58],[175,183],[489,496],[523,525],[533,535]],\"src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py\":[[1,27],[76,84],[91,96],[120,126],[140,145]],\"src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py\":[[1,51],[148,153],[172,179],[211,219],[268,278],[397,407],[443,452],[75,88],[91,105],[228,232],[307,309],[313,323],[358,363]],\"src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py\":[[1,35],[91,98],[134,138],[153,157],[185,197],[226,233],[283,286],[308,313],[353,361],[51,55],[62,64],[67,69],[76,79],[115,118],[121,124],[256,258],[271,273],[426,430]],\"src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py\":[[1,22],[97,104],[136,139],[159,163],[189,195],[215,220],[238,242],[272,283],[300,308],[400,403],[413,416],[429,433],[511,518],[64,71],[75,92],[175,178],[323,326],[616,623],[633,636],[663,666],[701,708],[712,715],[727,730],[765,767],[775,783]]}\nPFX = (\"noqa\", \"type:\", \"pyright:\", \"mypy:\", \"ruff:\", \"fmt:\", \"isort:\", \"pragma:\", \"nosec\", \"coverage:\", \"mechanism-ok:\", \"raw-git-ok:\", \"tickets-boundary-ok:\", \"read-via:\")\ndef normalize(src, path):\n    tree = ast.parse(src, filename=path, type_comments=True)\n    def visit(node, prefix=\"\"):\n        owner = \"module\" if isinstance(node, ast.Module) else prefix\n        body = getattr(node, \"body\", [])\n        if owner in DOCS[path] and body and isinstance(body[0], ast.Expr) and isinstance(body[0].value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(body[0].value.value, str):\n            body[0].value.value = \"__ALLOWLISTED_PROSE__\"\n        for child in body:\n            if isinstance(child, (ast.ClassDef, ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):\n                visit(child, f\"{prefix}.{child.name}\" if prefix else child.name)\n    visit(tree)\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node, ast.TypeIgnore):\n            node.lineno = 0\n    return ast.dump(tree, include_attributes=False)\ndef directives(src):\n    lines = src.splitlines()\n    out = []\n    for tok in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(src).readline):\n        if tok.type == tokenize.COMMENT:\n            body = tok.string[1:].lstrip().lower()\n            if tok.string.startswith(\"#!\") or any(body.startswith(p) for p in PFX):\n                out.append(lines[tok.start[0] - 1])\n    return out\nfor path in DOCS:\n    before = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"{B}:{path}\"], text=True)\n    final = Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    assert normalize(before, path) == normalize(final, path), (\"AST/runtime drift\", path)\n    assert directives(before) == directives(final), (\"directive/shebang drift\", path)\ndiff = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"diff\", \"--unified=0\", B, \"--\", *SPANS], text=True)\ncurrent = None\nfor line in diff.splitlines():\n    if line.startswith(\"+++ b/\"):\n        current = line[6:]\n    match = re.match(r\"^@@ -(\\d+)(?:,(\\d+))? \\+\\d+(?:,\\d+)? @@\", line)\n    if match:\n        start = int(match.group(1))\n        count = int(match.group(2) or \"1\")\n        allowed = SPANS[current]\n        if count:\n            assert all(any(lo <= n <= hi for lo, hi in allowed) for n in range(start, start + count)), (\"hunk outside allowlist\", current, start, count)\n        else:\n            assert any(lo <= start <= hi or lo <= start + 1 <= hi for lo, hi in allowed), (\"insertion outside allowlist\", current, start)\n'","dd_id":"immutable-prose-only","dd_text":"Only exact allowlisted prose changes: immutable-base runtime/non-comment structure and protected directives remain exact, and zero-context hunks stay inside base spans."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import subprocess; expected=set([\"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/guide_parity.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompt_library.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompt_model.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/__init__.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/run_failure.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/runner.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/step_failures.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/structured.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py\",\"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_verdict_cache.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/__init__.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/app.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/config.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py\",\"src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py\",\"docs/env-vars.md\"]); actual=set(subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--name-only\",\"HEAD^..HEAD\"],text=True).splitlines()); assert actual==expected,(actual,expected)'","dd_id":"exact-leaf-paths","dd_text":"The grouped commit changes exactly the 28 owned LLM and review-bot paths."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","dd_id":"comment-hygiene","dd_text":"The repository comment-hygiene policy passes."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest -q tests/unit/test_review_bot*.py tests/unit/test_reviewbot*.py tests/unit/review_bot tests/unit/test_reviewed_tree_binding_heldout_da31.py tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py tests/unit/test_code_review_artifact.py tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py tests/unit/test_git_timeout_bounds_77e1.py tests/unit/test_network_fetch_stall_abort_851e.py tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py","dd_id":"focused-contracts","dd_text":"Focused tests and build checks for every preserved subsystem consumer pass."},{"command":"rtk git diff --check HEAD^..HEAD -- src/rebar/review_bot/__init__.py src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py src/rebar/review_bot/app.py src/rebar/review_bot/config.py src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py","dd_id":"diff-integrity","dd_text":"The path-scoped patch contains no whitespace errors."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify","dd_id":"repository-gates","dd_text":"The complete local CI contract passes in the worktree virtualenv; do not apply a timeout."}]},"source_event_uuids":["4376f583-5fa0-4e82-8054-61b11c6d8bda","10935985-233d-4d50-9773-b9c301e9b64a","5698fa77-6e28-4702-8e71-296ad8780aee","02d0fd5e-c556-4cd6-b4be-3c1e63fc1505","94e00869-f66f-4757-ab2b-9805e54abba8","3825287d-bcd6-4aba-b923-0bd733be54d0","e4223b32-7260-46de-9c3f-5737fe362fda","3e14ff0e-aa90-471d-ad0c-bddb637d42c3","76e9763e-0e73-45b9-9091-e8c3d76ffb86","519959f3-0d2e-421b-a54c-cbd95e25aa45","d5e8b46f-7df4-44c3-8813-518a4e83bacd","216c7703-005d-4726-9862-f2e2c5730679","9df46bb2-1d18-4a86-a544-217c06375b27"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792779302457809860,"uuid":"595a0597-d8eb-435a-b80b-00380a76e756"}